WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.974
Sovereign AI means practical control over AI capability.

00:00:02.974 --> 00:00:04.052
In this course,

00:00:04.052 --> 00:00:08.363
it is not a vague political slogan and it is not limited

00:00:08.363 --> 00:00:11.238
to running a model on a local laptop.

00:00:11.238 --> 00:00:15.908
A sovereign AI program gives an organization deliberate control over where data goes,

00:00:15.908 --> 00:00:20.579
which models are approved, who can use them, what tools they can access,

00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:25.250
how outputs are reviewed, how logs are handled, and how changes are governed.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.842
Public AI tools can be useful for many low-risk workflows.

00:00:28.842 --> 00:00:32.794
Private AI systems may be necessary when data sensitivity, customer commitments,

00:00:32.794 --> 00:00:35.669
regulatory expectations, or operational ownership require tighter boundaries.

00:00:35.669 --> 00:00:39.621
Hybrid patterns may be the most realistic path for many teams,

00:00:39.621 --> 00:00:41.776
routing different work to local, private,

00:00:41.776 --> 00:00:45.728
or approved managed services based on data class and business need.

00:00:45.728 --> 00:00:47.884
The key idea is informed control.

00:00:47.884 --> 00:00:52.555
Teams need to understand the data, the model, the runtime, the access layer,

00:00:52.555 --> 00:00:56.148
the retrieval system, the monitoring plan, and the operational owner.

00:00:56.148 --> 00:00:57.225
Without that understanding,

00:00:57.225 --> 00:01:01.537
a system may feel private while still exposing sensitive prompts through logs,

00:01:01.537 --> 00:01:04.770
unmanaged embeddings, broad tool permissions, or unclear vendor settings.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:08.004
Sovereign AI is therefore an engineering and governance discipline.

00:01:08.004 --> 00:01:10.878
It combines infrastructure, security, privacy, policy, cost management,

00:01:10.878 --> 00:01:12.315
and user workflow design.

00:01:12.315 --> 00:01:15.549
The goal is not to make every system isolated.

00:01:15.549 --> 00:01:19.860
The goal is to make every AI workflow intentional, reviewable, and maintainable.
